  "auditor": "trapi:gpt-5.6-sol_2026-07-09",
  "claims": [
    {
      "text": "Equiatomic NbZrTiHfMo forms a disordered BCC solid solution.",
      "field": "material_initial_state",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Equiatomic NbZrTiHfMo has a room-temperature compressive yield strength of 1719 MPa.",
      "field": "material_initial_state",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Equiatomic NbZrTiHfMo has limited room-temperature compressive plasticity.",
      "field": "material_initial_state",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The high Mo content in equiatomic NbZrTiHfMo increases the inter-element electronegativity difference and contributes to its limited plasticity.",
      "field": "material_initial_state",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Replacing 50% of the Mo with V produces NbZrTiHf(Mo0.5V0.5), corresponding to Nb20Zr20Ti20Hf20Mo10V10 in atomic percent.",
      "field": "intervention",
      "needs_support": false,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Partial replacement of Mo by V will reduce the overall electronegativity mismatch.",
      "field": "hypothesis",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The V-substituted alloy will retain a disordered BCC solid solution at suitable substitution levels.",
      "field": "structural_mediator",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "V has a lower electronegativity than Mo.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Reducing the electronegativity mismatch by adding V will decrease bond distortion and chemical heterogeneity.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Decreased bond distortion and chemical heterogeneity will enhance dislocation mobility.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Enhanced dislocation mobility will improve room-temperature compressive plasticity.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The refractory nature of the alloy system will preserve most of its high yield strength after partial Mo-to-V substitution.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "At the targeted substitution level, plastic strain will improve by more than 10% relative to equiatomic NbZrTiHfMo.",
      "field": "predicted_outcome",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "At the targeted substitution level, compressive yield strength will decrease by less than approximately 10% from 1719 MPa.",
      "field": "predicted_outcome",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The beneficial strength-plasticity effect depends on retention of the BCC phase.",
      "field": "boundary",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Excessive substitution of V for Mo could trigger phase changes or substantially reduce yield strength.",
      "field": "boundary",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC10785334::page::001"
      ],
      "same_system": "no"
    },
    {
      "text": "Changing elemental composition can alter whether an HEA exhibits FCC, BCC, or mixed phase constitution.",
      "field": "boundary",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "entailed",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC10785334::page::001"
      ],
      "same_system": "no"
    },
    {
      "text": "A composition series with x = 0, 0.25, 0.50, 0.75, and 1.0, tested by room-temperature compression and characterized by XRD and TEM, can evaluate the proposed response and phase retention.",
      "field": "falsification_experiment.design",
      "needs_support": false,
